&lt;p&gt;🌱 We were founded in 2007&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💰 We have provided over $3bn of funding to small businesses so far&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🚀 We have been named in&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CNBC &amp;amp; Statista Top 150 UK Fintechs for 2025&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌍 We&#39;re a global team, with a dynamic presence in&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;key locations around the world&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🧠 We&#39;re a thriving community of over&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;290&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;innovative minds&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;👩🏾 🤝 👨🏼 We&#39;re a vibrant melting pot, celebrating over&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;27&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;nationalities in our team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🏢 Our team brings experience from over&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;740&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;previous companies, from startups to global giants&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🎯 We have just been named as one of&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FinTech’s Finest 50&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;by Welcome to the Jungle&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;💪 We’re proud to be an accredited&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Real Living Wage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;employer, ensuring everyone is paid fairly for the great work they do!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Product &amp;amp; Engineering Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liberis is building the embedded finance platform that lets partners around the world offer innovative funding products to their small business customers. We&#39;re a growth-stage fintech with teams in London, Nottingham, Atlanta, Stockholm, Munich and Mumbai, and we’re building a global Product, Data &amp;amp; Engineering team that thrives on autonomy, ownership, and is focused on impact! Our teams solve real-world problems for small businesses, shaping products that unlock opportunity at scale.&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering is going through an AI-first transformation, rethinking how teams are structured and how they ship. It&#39;s changing what a small team can do! We empower our teams to make decisions, move fast, and take full responsibility for the solutions they deliver. You’ll join a team where curiosity is encouraged and collaboration across Product, Data, Delivery and Engineering is the norm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Salesforce team:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join Liberis&#39; Salesforce Engineering practice, which owns and evolves the Salesforce platform behind how Liberis acquires, onboards, and supports merchants and partners across 15 markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll build and run your own pod of up to four people, drawn from developers and admins. This role sits within the wider Technology function and work closely with product teams and business functions such as commercial and operations to turn business needs into reliable Salesforce solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The role:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Salesforce Engineering Lead is a people leader role that stays hands-on. You&#39;ll own the technical direction of your team&#39;s part of the Salesforce org and the growth of the people in it. This isn&#39;t a step away from engineering into pure management. Liberis expects both.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roughly 60-70% of your time goes to technical and delivery leadership, 20-30% to people management (1:1s, performance, career development, hiring), and the rest to cross-team and strategic work. The exact split depends on where your team is and what it needs at the time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical direction and quality of your team&#39;s part of the Salesforce org: object model, security and sharing, automation, and integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make or guide architecture decisions with clear reasoning about the trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close enough to the code to review it credibly, help with the hard problems, and lead incident response when something breaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the line on engineering practice: CI/CD, Salesforce DX, testing, code review, and release management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set goals, give feedback, and support career development for developers and admins at different levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a team environment where people can grow and where feedback runs both ways.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Delivery and stakeholder partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with sales, operations, and other customer-facing teams to understand how they work and where Salesforce can do more for them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with other engineering teams to coordinate integrations and provide best-practice guidance on using Salesforce APIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic advisor, not just an order-taker: help teams rethink a process, not just build what they first asked for.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the Salesforce roadmap and make sure changes are scalable and lined up with the wider business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own platform health: security, data quality, and governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adoption of automation, including AI-driven automation, that cuts cost to serve without cutting quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent your team&#39;s technical view in cross-team and leadership discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we think you&#39;ll need:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in a Salesforce development role, including time spent owning architecture decisions rather than just implementing them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep command of Apex, Lightning Web Components, and SOQL/SOSL, plus confident declarative configuration: Flow, object modelling, validation rules, security and sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating Salesforce with external systems through REST/SOAP APIs and platform events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Some experience leading, mentoring, or managing other developers or admins, even informally, and a genuine interest in doing more of it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of improving sales or operations processes, not just maintaining what&#39;s already there.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working directly with sales, operations, and other non-technical stakeholders: understanding what they need, challenging assumptions, and explaining trade-offs in plain terms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with version control (we use GitHub), CI/CD, and Salesforce DX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Salesforce Application Architect or System Architect certification, or clearly working towards one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broader tooling perspective: experience with related platforms such as Braze, Zendesk, or marketing and workflow automation tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a technology company, ideally in or around embedded finance or fintech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within and across software engineering teams, not just inside a Salesforce silo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong interest in AI-driven automation and where it can reduce manual work and cost to serve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Liberis is an equal opportunities employer. We welcome applications from all candidates, including individuals with disabilities and provide reasonable adjustments as required.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our hybrid approach&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working together in person helps us move faster, collaborate better, and build a great Liberis culture. Our hybrid working policy requires team members to be in the office at least 3 days a week. At Liberis, we embrace flexibility as a core part of our culture, while also valuing the importance of the time our teams spend together in the office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;#LI-FC1&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;Find more English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom on Arbeitnow

